# A companion bled dry leaves the party, and leaves a body — the same as one cut down.
#
# The Starvation arm of PartyMember.CauseOfDeath, and the one that was wrong twice over. Humor
# depletion is recorded on the Fighter wrapper (Fighter.IsHumorDepleted), which the fight throws away,
# so a bled-out companion was not dead by any measure the world could read — and nothing removed a
# dead companion from the party anyway. What survives the fight is the humor queues themselves, which
# really are empty, so the sweep reads Starvation off state that was there all along.
#
# See companion_death_wounds.cli for the shared half of this (the modal notice, the body, the party
# removal) and for why `fight-wound` and `fight-deplete` exist at all. What is asserted here and
# nowhere else is the CAUSE: the notice must say the humors, not the wounds, because getting the two
# confused is exactly the failure — a companion at full hit points reading as unhurt.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only brewer --auto-dialogue

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

inspect party
expect-state party Nighthunter

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The landed attack HOLDS the fight so its first blow can be read (see "Opening a fight: the first
# blow"). The fight opens on the press that closes the segment, not on the swing.
click button
wait mode Fighting 90

# Humors, not hit points: `fight-deplete` empties the queues the way a terminal bleed does and raises
# the wrapper flag the way BleedingEffect's last tick does. The companion's hit points never move.
fight-deplete Nighthunter
wait 20

# Still a fight — one dead party member is not a defeat while the protagonist stands.
wait mode Fighting 20

fight-end victory
wait 90

# Named by what actually killed them. A wounds line here would mean the cause was guessed from the
# fact of the death rather than read off the body.
expect Nighthunter
expect bled out, humors spent

click companion-death
wait 60
advance 12 180

inspect party
expect-no-state party Nighthunter
inspect pois
expect-state pois Nighthunter's Remains

quit
